s of test cases, starting with a \"前置条件\" (preconditions) section that describes the system state before the test runs, including database and cache details.\n\nContinuing with the input parameters section, which specifies the exact values passed to the system being tested, including boundary cases like empty strings, nil values, and negative numbers that should trigger error handling.\n\nThen the operation sequence section that outlines the steps to execute in order, beginning with establishing preconditions and then performing the actual test operations.\n\nThe expected output section describes the observable results we should verify, including return values with their specific types, state changes in storage, any errors or exceptions thrown with their messages or codes, and events or logs emitted.\n\nFinally, I'm noting common anti-patterns to avoid in test cases, such as vague preconditions that don't specify all field values, or unclear expected outputs.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c200e74-95d8-4d6d-9878-97ef17b8029a","uuid":"3c389564-044a-487c-9670-5b20d113d495"}
